{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"362e9f66bf03a952","type":"text","text":"[summary]\n\nFocus on ONLY Generative AI in fundraising for nonprofits.\n### Module 2: Fundraising\n**Learning Outcomes:**\n1. Understand the fundamentals of fundraising in the nonprofit sector.\n2. Learn how to use generative AI to identify and engage potential donors.\n3. Develop skills in creating persuasive fundraising materials using AI.\n\n**Necessary Content:**\n- Overview of fundraising strategies and best practices.\n- Introduction to generative AI tools relevant to fundraising, like donor segmentation, personalized communication, and content creation.\n- Techniques for crafting effective fundraising appeals, campaigns, and donor stewardship programs using AI.\n\n**Generative AI Use Cases:**\n- Donor Research: Employing AI to analyze and segment donor data for targeted outreach.\n- Campaign Creation: Generating engaging content for fundraising campaigns, including emails, social media posts, and grant proposals.\n- Personalization: Using AI to tailor communications and build relationships with donors, enhancing donor engagement and retention.","x":-1560,"y":-194,"width":540,"height":914},
		{"id":"b721d13b70d028de","type":"text","text":"[topic]\nGenerative AI, ChatGPT nonprofit management, fundraising","x":-960,"y":-194,"width":340,"height":794},
		{"id":"61eba20dfe5938a4","type":"text","text":"[KB]\n\n{{[[Nonprofit Management (Course)]]}}","x":-41,"y":-194,"width":721,"height":754},
		{"id":"cb0c5985b7580195","type":"text","text":"[course]\n{{[[AI for Nonprofit Management (Outline)]]}}","x":-340,"y":109,"width":250,"height":264},
		{"id":"fd15b5781ca74dcf","type":"text","text":"[mod]\nModule 2\n","x":-620,"y":109,"width":250,"height":127},
		{"id":"b899d8fd05e60755","type":"text","text":"[Tone]\nProfessional, educational, engaging, practical.\n\nShow don't tell.","x":-620,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"e4ce0f2c27c7ebf7","type":"text","text":"[skills]\n\n1. **AI Literacy**: Understanding the basics of artificial intelligence, including how generative AI operates and can be applied in various nonprofit management contexts such as program development, fundraising, stewardship, and grant writing/reporting.\n    \n2. **Data Analysis and Interpretation**: Skills in analyzing and interpreting data to inform decision-making, especially in the context of donor research, program impact assessment, and identifying grant opportunities.\n    \n3. **Strategic Thinking and Planning**: Ability to use AI tools for strategic planning, including developing logic models for program development, creating targeted fundraising strategies, and planning personalized donor stewardship approaches.\n    \n4. **Creative Problem-Solving**: Leveraging AI for ideation and design, requiring creativity to solve problems and innovate within program development, fundraising campaigns, and donor engagement strategies.\n    \n5. **Technical Proficiency with AI Tools**: Competence in navigating and utilizing specific AI tools and platforms that assist in tasks such as donor segmentation, content creation for fundraising, and automated reporting.\n    \n6. **Communication and Persuasion**: Skills in crafting persuasive and engaging content with the help of AI, including writing grant proposals, fundraising appeals, and personalized donor communications.\n    \n7. **Project Management**: Managing projects effectively, from the ideation phase with AI through to execution, including organizing fundraising campaigns, overseeing program development, and handling grant reporting processes.\n    \n8. **Ethical Consideration and Bias Awareness**: Understanding the ethical implications of using AI in nonprofit management, including issues related to data privacy, donor consent, and being aware of and mitigating biases in AI-generated content and decision-making processes.\n","x":895,"y":-823,"width":810,"height":1783},
		{"id":"6b08fd22e19786b1","type":"text","text":"{{[[Project Creator]]}} create a project for {{outline}}","x":-3920,"y":4363,"width":250,"height":197,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e206a944b2d106de","type":"text","text":"### Module 2: Fundraising with Generative AI in Nonprofits\n\n#### 2.1 Rationale: The Importance of AI in Modern Fundraising\n- Understanding the competitive edge AI brings to fundraising.\n- Recognizing how AI can enhance donor relationships and increase funding.\n- Relating AI advancements to the nonprofit sector's need for efficiency and personalization.\n\n#### 2.2 Expectations: Skills to Master in AI-Enhanced Fundraising\n- Ability to identify and utilize AI tools for donor engagement and segmentation.\n- Proficiency in creating AI-generated fundraising materials that resonate with donors.\n- Skills in developing and managing AI-assisted fundraising campaigns.\n\n#### 2.3 Pre-Assessment: Gauge Your AI Fundraising Readiness\n- Multiple Choice: Identifying the benefits of using AI in fundraising.\n- Fill in the Blank: Understanding terms related to AI and fundraising.\n- Scenario-Based Questions: Selecting the best AI approach for a given fundraising challenge.\n  - Feedback will direct learners to specific module sections based on incorrect responses.\n\n#### 2.4 Concepts and Theories: Foundations of AI in Fundraising\n- Generative AI: Definition, operation, and application in donor communications.\n- Data-Driven Fundraising: How AI analyzes and uses donor data for better outreach.\n- AI in Content Creation: Theories behind automated content generation for campaigns.\n\n#### 2.5 Walkthrough: Implementing AI in Your Fundraising Strategy\n- Step-by-step guide on segmenting donor data using AI tools.\n- Detailed process for creating personalized donor communications with AI.\n- Instructions on setting up and launching an AI-powered fundraising campaign.\n\n#### 2.6 Best Practices: Effective Use of AI in Nonprofit Fundraising\n- Personalization: Best practices for tailoring donor communications with AI.\n- Transparency and Trust: Maintaining donor trust when using AI in fundraising.\n- Continuous Learning: Staying updated on AI trends and tools in the nonprofit sector.\n\n#### 2.7 Case Study: AI Transforms a Fundraising Campaign\n- Scenario: A mid-sized nonprofit adopting AI to revitalize its annual fundraising.\n- Process: How the organization implemented generative AI in its strategy.\n- Outcome: Analysis of the campaign's success and lessons learned.\n\n#### 2.8 Application: Hands-on with AI in Fundraising\n- Practice Activity: Crafting a donor appeal email using generative AI.\n- Role-Play: Engaging with a chatbot to simulate donor queries and AI responses.\n- Scenario Exercise: Planning an AI-assisted fundraising event from start to finish.","x":120,"y":1880,"width":1640,"height":1600,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"6d4cb37e40c281eb","type":"text","text":"[audience]\nAdult learners looking to upskill or for a career change\n\nLittle or no experience with AI or Generative AI tools, so they need a lot of guidance and examples.\n\nThe audience will NOT be training models, only using available ones like chatgpt.","x":-340,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"18795c84f0d61402","type":"text","text":"#### 2.1 Rationale: The Importance of AI in Modern Fundraising\n\nIn the current non-profit sector, the effective mobilization of resources is paramount. Integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) into fundraising strategies offers significant advantages that can elevate the impact of your organization. Here's why understanding AI's role in fundraising is crucial:\n\nFirstly, AI provides a competitive edge by automating and optimizing tasks that traditionally consume considerable time and resources. For instance, AI can sift through vast amounts of data to identify potential donors more effectively than any human team could. This efficiency not only saves time but also allows your organization to allocate resources more strategically.\n\nSecondly, AI's ability to enhance donor relationships is a game-changer. By analyzing donor behaviors and preferences, AI can help tailor communications and appeals to individual interests, increasing the likelihood of donations. This level of personalization fosters a stronger connection between donors and your cause, which is critical in building a loyal supporter base.\n\nLastly, in a sector where every penny counts, the need for efficiency and personalization is not just a luxury but a necessity. AI advancements meet this need by enabling your nonprofit to craft targeted campaigns, streamline operations, and ensure that your message resonates with the right audience at the right time.\n\nEmbracing AI in fundraising is about staying ahead in a rapidly changing environment. It's about maximizing potential in every campaign and interaction with donors. Your mission is meaningful – and harnessing the power of AI can help you convey that message more powerfully than ever before.","x":-2600,"y":1880,"width":888,"height":1147,"color":"6"},
